# 🚩 Challenge: [2warm]

## 📝 Challenge Description
![base2binary](../2warm.png)
Q.Can you convert the number 42 (base 10) to binary (base 2)?

hints:
1. Submit your answer in our competition's flag format. For example, if your answer was '11111', you would submit 'academy{11111}' as the flag.

## 🚀  Solution 
Detail your step-by-step breakdown to get the flag:
1. python 
$ python3 -c "print(bin(42))"
or 
2. linux cmdline
$ echo "obase=2; 42" | bc
101010


## 🏁 Flag
academy{101010}
